---
import Tool from '../../layouts/Tool.astro';
import MpePlayground from '../../components/MpePlayground.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
---

<Tool slug="mpe" wide description="See MPE in your browser: per-note pitch bend, pressure and timbre (CC 74) from your controller or a simulated performance, with zones and a message log.">
  <Fragment slot="lede">
    MPE gives every note its own MIDI channel, so each one can bend, swell and change tone independently. Connect
    an MPE controller to see each note's pitch, pressure and timbre move, or watch a simulated performance.
  </Fragment>
  <MpePlayground />
  <Callout slot="after" title="What you're seeing">
    <p>
      Each circle is one note on its own member channel. Its horizontal position is the note plus that channel's pitch
      bend (±48 semitones by default in MPE) plus the zone's manager-channel bend. Height is CC 74 (timbre) and size is
      channel pressure. The tick at the bottom marks the key that was struck.
    </p>
  </Callout>
</Tool>
